s of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$", ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=11,$ and since $B$ is formed by $4$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 4+\\text{nullity}(A) & =11 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =11-4 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$", ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/id": "59ca9559-bc72-5951-9d03-d0431c559f1b", ":answer-field/key": "selection", ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio", ":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "469941d9-dd44-598e-b8ad-f8efa3eec06b", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "6"}, {":answer/id": "e9d7c353-5192-5bb7-8c35-6ce5e50b5d02", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "7"}, {":answer/id": "82412796-7615-5739-bdd1-a1d8f3511da6", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "8"}, {":answer/id": "c0b9e891-c618-5763-ad8c-f09e3138d44e", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "9"}, {":answer/id": "df075768-d5fc-5374-a795-327a5b073c3d", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "10"}], ":answer-field/correct": [":answer/id", "e9d7c353-5192-5bb7-8c35-6ce5e50b5d02"]}]}, "generation": {"version": "rank-nullity-description-v1", "seed": 718113670, "template": "column-basis", "profile": "offset-minus1", "parameters": {"m": 4, "n": 11, "k": 4}, "correct_value": "7", "mathematical_fingerprint": "8d26417765190d5b85673b2c82a29b3f24b01045fa3e503447523a32a31e74a0", "content_fingerprint": "98a1b313d1d5dfedee83700fe609f37d2b382247c339f634667c971761cd0937", "source_question_ids": ["q-142487"], "source_basis": 2516, "source_lineage": "01a12a15-3e0a-75a1-9dac-f8b8c5d5c3f1", "dependencies": {"python": "3.13.5", "sympy": "1.14.0"}, "plots": "none", "domain": "real vector spaces; full column rank parameter coefficient matrix", "math_format": "course-academy-tex-v1"}}, "checks": [{"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "469941d9-dd44-598e-b8ad-f8efa3eec06b", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "e9d7c353-5192-5bb7-8c35-6ce5e50b5d02", "expected": "accepted", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "82412796-7615-5739-bdd1-a1d8f3511da6", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "c0b9e891-c618-5763-ad8c-f09e3138d44e", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "df075768-d5fc-5374-a795-327a5b073c3d", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}]}, {"label": "78d6a8a8-7bc9-5be5-a16c-f92da9337296", "record": {"knowledge_point": {"db_id": 17592186184171, "id": "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe", "title": "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}, "question": {":question/id": "78d6a8a8-7bc9-5be5-a16c-f92da9337296", ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate", ":question/problem": "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.\n$$", ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$", ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/id": "f2c33d6a-3793-5b7d-a36d-ada017b31469", ":answer-field/key": "selection", ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio", ":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "f6209992-9a29-570c-8beb-3f2692a8cda4", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "1"}, {":answer/id": "f635adf2-4176-5e44-84ae-2fb7541566a0", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "2"}, {":answer/id": "6d890b8d-3401-5a60-89a8-038a12057ec3", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "3"}, {":answer/id": "54334815-3d70-5747-8179-5efb06fac933", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "4"}, {":answer/id": "476c3ce3-dfb7-5c51-bb2b-9aa1680f1ae4", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "5"}], ":answer-field/correct": [":answer/id", "f635adf2-4176-5e44-84ae-2fb7541566a0"]}]}, "generation": {"version": "rank-nullity-description-v1", "seed": 718113666, "template": "null-space-display", "profile": "one-through5", "parameters": {"matrix": [[-1, 0], [-1, 1], [0, 0], [-1, -1]], "indices": [2, 3]}, "correct_value": "2", "mathematical_fingerprint": "b6891845a285bd22ab4f00f64624b861c11e843161a9932282e83cae9e842429", "content_fingerprint": "3a9bb29cbf34eabebe1ad75c49ed00566b9a4f0f6c05197246dc42bfd27b2082", "source_question_ids": ["q-35306", "q-35434"], "source_basis": 2516, "source_lineage": "01a12a15-3e0a-75a1-9dac-f8b8c5d5c3f1", "dependencies": {"python": "3.13.5", "sympy": "1.14.0"}, "plots": "none", "domain": "real vector spaces; full column rank parameter coefficient matrix", "math_format": "course-academy-tex-v1"}}, "checks": [{"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "f6209992-9a29-570c-8beb-3f2692a8cda4", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "f635adf2-4176-5e44-84ae-2fb7541566a0", "expected": "accepted", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "6d890b8d-3401-5a60-89a8-038a12057ec3", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "54334815-3d70-5747-8179-5efb06fac933", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "476c3ce3-dfb7-5c51-bb2b-9aa1680f1ae4", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}]}, {"label": "b27cc37a-1e00-5199-bb4b-8ba97611aaf6", "record": {"knowledge_point": {"db_id": 17592186184171, "id": "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe", "title": "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}, "question": {":question/id": "b27cc37a-1e00-5199-bb4b-8ba97611aaf6", ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate", ":question/problem": "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.$", ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$", ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/id": "582c2a41-21d6-5067-98a1-674cd11c3876", ":answer-field/key": "selection", ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio", ":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "7cd6c756-05c6-530c-a2c1-98411204467d", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "1"}, {":answer/id": "17003112-d083-588c-9060-34db195c97b9", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "2"}, {":answer/id": "e73dfbcb-1ca9-5d70-a674-1882594cda87", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "3"}, {":answer/id": "ed5dec0d-87a8-58bd-b1e9-25fc30d37721", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "4"}, {":answer/id": "2018c058-c1b0-5089-9cde-fcdedfb6333f", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "5"}], ":answer-field/correct": [":answer/id", "7cd6c756-05c6-530c-a2c1-98411204467d"]}]}, "generation": {"version": "rank-nullity-description-v1", "seed": 718113667, "template": "null-space-inline", "profile": "one-through5", "parameters": {"matrix": [[0, 0, -3], [-2, 3, -2], [0, 0, 0], [3, -2, 0]], "indices": [1, 2, 3]}, "correct_value": "1", "mathematical_fingerprint": "301f5285511e065abaa2f6d0be68ddb71a64c54ba1f6a17b271ca9aa8b56b4d6", "content_fingerprint": "4878c652f6bdbbf60930fa999eef0b8cc7be5017cd9cb448752722dc2013ed1f", "source_question_ids": ["q-35306", "q-35434"], "source_basis": 2516, "source_lineage": "01a12a15-3e0a-75a1-9dac-f8b8c5d5c3f1", "dependencies": {"python": "3.13.5", "sympy": "1.14.0"}, "plots": "none", "domain": "real vector spaces; full column rank parameter coefficient matrix", "math_format": "course-academy-tex-v1"}}, "checks": [{"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "7cd6c756-05c6-530c-a2c1-98411204467d", "expected": "accepted", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "submitted_answer_id": "17003112-d083-588c-9060-34db195c97b9", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all five radio choices through actual grader"}, {"field_index": 0, "